  "transcript": [
    {
      "start": 138.99,
      "end": 211.72,
      "text": "This is Tommy Vance on Radio 1.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 211.74,
      "end": 216.47,
      "text": "And light the lasers in your heart",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 216.47,
      "end": 222.11,
      "text": "For all the world to see",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 222.11,
      "end": 225.11,
      "text": "Exactly 11 minutes past 11.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 350.0,
      "end": 352.9,
      "text": "That was the Friday Night Connection put together by Richard Ransom",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 352.9,
      "end": 355.74,
      "text": "of Seaman Close, Park Streets and Albards in Hertfordshire.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 357.7,
      "end": 358.52,
      "text": "Three bits of music.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 358.8,
      "end": 359.9,
      "text": "The connection is in there somewhere.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 360.06,
      "end": 363.06,
      "text": "It could be the name of the artist, name of the song, name of the album,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 363.38,
      "end": 364.26,
      "text": "name of the record company.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 364.36,
      "end": 366.16,
      "text": "It could be anywhere that it's in there somewhere.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 366.46,
      "end": 367.24,
      "text": "I promise you.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 367.84,
      "end": 373.3,
      "text": "Any ideas, if you have, jot them down",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 374.69,
      "end": 380.03,
      "text": "On the back of an envelope, postcard, anything you like, as long as it is a written communication, and send it to",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 380.03,
      "end": 387.23,
      "text": "The Friday Night Connection, The Friday Rock Show, BBC, Radio 1, London, W1A4WW.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 388.01,
      "end": 397.98,
      "text": "The address, once again, is The Friday Night Connection, The Friday Rock Show, BBC, Radio 1, London, W1A4WW.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 399.76,
      "end": 403.6,
      "text": "The prize, a 12-pound record token, and a few other goodies, and the best of luck.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 403.6,
      "end": 408.88,
      "text": "It certainly is, and now it's 12 minutes past 11.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 408.98,
      "end": 410.46,
      "text": "OK, I'm going to play a little game with you now.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 410.56,
      "end": 412.56,
      "text": "I'm going to play you four pieces of music.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 412.76,
      "end": 413.68,
      "text": "Four pieces of music.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 413.9,
      "end": 418.98,
      "text": "One of them came out in 65, one 66, one was certainly recorded pre-67,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 419.36,
      "end": 422.02,
      "text": "and one was recorded about 1968.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 422.9,
      "end": 427.3,
      "text": "These four bits of music are all to do with the history of musicians",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 427.3,
      "end": 431.26,
      "text": "who were in a very, very famous band who are, or rather who have,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 431.26,
      "end": 435.34,
      "text": "just announced that they are going to reform, and it has been confirmed.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 435.34,
      "end": 438.98,
      "text": "I'm not going to tell you who they are until after these four records.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 439.64,
      "end": 441.3,
      "text": "No clues, no nothing.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 441.62,
      "end": 442.78,
      "text": "See if you can work it out.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 443.4,
      "end": 447.6,
      "text": "Relate to five musicians, right, five musicians,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1307.1,
      "end": 1308.72,
      "text": "one of them a singer as well,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1309.94,
      "end": 1312.88,
      "text": "who were in a very, very, very famous band",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1312.88,
      "end": 1316.28,
      "text": "who did their first gig in the Mark II version",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1316.28,
      "end": 1318.44,
      "text": "on the 10th of June 1969",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1318.44,
      "end": 1322.12,
      "text": "in a club which I can virtually see from the studio in London,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1322.12,
      "end": 1324.98,
      "text": "and their last gig as the Mark II version",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1324.98,
      "end": 1328.12,
      "text": "on the 29th of June, 1973.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1328.94,
      "end": 1330.18,
      "text": "I'm not going to tell you who they are yet,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1330.22,
      "end": 1331.72,
      "text": "but that last one could have given it away.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1332.18,
      "end": 1334.12,
      "text": "The bands you just heard were Episode 6,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1334.62,
      "end": 1336.66,
      "text": "The Artwoods, MI5,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1336.9,
      "end": 1339.92,
      "text": "and the first record was the Something Something Orchestra.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1340.2,
      "end": 1341.34,
      "text": "If I told you the Something Something,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1341.58,
      "end": 1343.42,
      "text": "that would give it away entirely.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1343.88,
      "end": 1345.3,
      "text": "And now here's a couple of tracks",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1345.3,
      "end": 1348.28,
      "text": "from the first BBC session that they recorded",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1348.28,
      "end": 1349.7,
      "text": "as the Mark II version,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1350.04,
      "end": 1352.78,
      "text": "and they recorded it on the 11th of August, 1969,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1352.96,
      "end": 1354.48,
      "text": "and this definitely will give it away.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1354.98,
      "end": 1357.66,
      "text": "Give away the answer, and what is the answer?",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1357.84,
      "end": 1361.34,
      "text": "Well, this band have reformed, and it is now confirmed news.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1361.34,
      "end": 1721.02,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 1721.02,
      "end": 1726.16,
      "text": "Recorded in the studios of the BBC on the 11th of August 1969, some 15 years ago,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1726.6,
      "end": 1729.28,
      "text": "and engineered, incidentally, by Tony Wilson, producer of this programme,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1729.4,
      "end": 1731.06,
      "text": "when he was a young man and just an engineer,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1731.2,
      "end": 1733.4,
      "text": "when he used to twiddle the knobs before he became a producer.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1734.06,
      "end": 1736.0,
      "text": "And I would imagine that's given it all away now.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1736.0,
      "end": 1739.4,
      "text": "The numbers you heard were This Bird Has Flown and Ricochet.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1739.62,
      "end": 1741.32,
      "text": "No, it wasn't speaking, it was Ricochet.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1741.84,
      "end": 1744.38,
      "text": "The band are Deep Purple, and the news is out,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1744.5,
      "end": 1747.04,
      "text": "they are definitely reforming in the Mark II version.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1747.62,
      "end": 1751.92,
      "text": "Ian Gillan, Ian Pace, John Lord, Roger Glover and Ritchie Blackmore.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1752.44,
      "end": 1754.74,
      "text": "They are shortly to start rehearsals for an album.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1755.28,
      "end": 1757.26,
      "text": "Then they're going to do their recording session, obviously.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1757.44,
      "end": 1760.08,
      "text": "The album will be released late summer or in the autumn.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1760.68,
      "end": 1764.02,
      "text": "A world tour will commence at the end of the year or the beginning of next year.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1764.02,
      "end": 1766.66,
      "text": "they're looking at it as a long-term project",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1766.66,
      "end": 1768.08,
      "text": "not just a sort of one-off deal",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1768.08,
      "end": 1770.26,
      "text": "and the tracks, the early tracks you heard",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1770.26,
      "end": 1771.64,
      "text": "that I played were Episode 6",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1771.64,
      "end": 1774.16,
      "text": "the band that incorporated Glover and Gillen",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1774.16,
      "end": 1775.32,
      "text": "the track was Mr. Universe",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1775.32,
      "end": 1777.44,
      "text": "then you heard The Artwoods",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1777.44,
      "end": 1779.24,
      "text": "and a track called Walk on the Wild Side",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1779.24,
      "end": 1780.38,
      "text": "John Lord on the Keyboards",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1780.38,
      "end": 1782.5,
      "text": "before that, MI5",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1782.5,
      "end": 1784.52,
      "text": "a band that was also known as The Maze",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1784.52,
      "end": 1786.7,
      "text": "that incorporated Mr. Ian Pace on the drums",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1786.7,
      "end": 1789.1,
      "text": "the track was called You'll Never Stop Me Loving You",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1789.1,
      "end": 1790.18,
      "text": "and before that you heard",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1790.18,
      "end": 1792.14,
      "text": "the Ritchie Blackmore Orchestra",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1792.14,
      "end": 1795.12,
      "text": "and a thing entitled Little Brown Jug.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1795.58,
      "end": 1797.2,
      "text": "Spoke to Ian Gillan on the phone yesterday.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1797.36,
      "end": 1800.5,
      "text": "He's over the moon about it, and so am I.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1800.5,
      "end": 2523.35,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 1905.98,
      "end": 1911.38,
      "text": "Recorded back in 1972, the album was Deep Purple,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2523.35,
      "end": 2525.73,
      "text": "made in Japan, the track Child in Time.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2528.17,
      "end": 2530.61,
      "text": "Just in case you're only, well, at this moment of time,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2530.61,
      "end": 2532.53,
      "text": "rolling out the pub and you haven't heard Deep Purple.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2533.19,
      "end": 2536.85,
      "text": "Mark Two are definitely reforming and getting it back together again.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2536.95,
      "end": 2540.11,
      "text": "Ian Gillan, Ian Pace, John Lord, Roger Glover and Richie Blackmore.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2540.65,
      "end": 2543.37,
      "text": "Start rehearsals for an album soon, and then they do the session.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2543.51,
      "end": 2545.01,
      "text": "The album will be out summer-autumn.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2545.51,
      "end": 2547.97,
      "text": "World tour commencing at the end of this year, beginning of next year,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2548.35,
      "end": 2549.41,
      "text": "and best of luck to them.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2549.81,
      "end": 2551.65,
      "text": "And Ian told me something else that's very nice.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2551.69,
      "end": 2553.27,
      "text": "If you look at photographs of Deep Purple,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2553.93,
      "end": 2556.55,
      "text": "you see behind them the amp stacks, the amplifiers, right?",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2556.55,
      "end": 2559.95,
      "text": "And on them, written the name Marshall, Marshall Amp Stacks.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2560.59,
      "end": 2563.07,
      "text": "Well, Ian told me yesterday that Jim Marshall of that company",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2563.07,
      "end": 2566.37,
      "text": "has just been awarded the Queen's Award for Industry,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2566.49,
      "end": 2567.77,
      "text": "or to Industry, whichever it's called.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2567.95,
      "end": 2569.13,
      "text": "Congratulations, Mr Marshall.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2569.77,
      "end": 2571.63,
      "text": "And it's great to have Deep Purple back,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2571.75,
      "end": 2575.05,
      "text": "who always show up so distinctly in our birthday programmes,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2575.33,
      "end": 2576.47,
      "text": "based on your votes.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2576.99,
      "end": 2577.63,
      "text": "Nice one.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    }
  ]
}